== Bài 5A (220 từ – Chủ đề Unit 1 & Unit 2)
*Read the following passage and mark the letter A, B, C, or D to indicate the correct answer to each of the questions.*

#passage-box[
  In many Vietnamese households today, traditional gender roles are changing in a positive and balanced way. In the past, fathers were usually the sole breadwinners while mothers stayed home to manage all cooking, cleaning, and childcare. Nowadays, with both parents working demanding full-time jobs, sharing housework equally has become essential for maintaining a peaceful, supportive home.

  Furthermore, modern families are combining daily chores with eco-friendly habits to protect the natural environment. In Minh's family in Vinh City, every member follows a clear weekly schedule. Minh and his younger sister sort household waste into organic food scraps and recyclable items before putting out the rubbish each evening. When doing the grocery shopping at the local market, his mother always brings a reusable woven basket instead of taking dozens of single-use plastic bags. Meanwhile, his father checks all electrical appliances and reminds everyone to turn #underline[#strong[them]] off whenever nobody is in the room.

  Practicing green routines together brings two wonderful long-term benefits. First, #underline[#strong[spotless]] living spaces and lower monthly electricity bills make family life much more comfortable and economical. Second, children naturally develop practical life skills, deep gratitude, and strong environmental awareness from an early age. Instead of viewing chores as a tiring daily burden, Minh's family treats housework as meaningful teamwork that cares for both their beloved home and the planet.
]

